1 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Two people can walk away from the same experience with completely different stories. </p><p>One replays it all evening, simmering. The other has already moved on. Same event, different state of mind.</p><p>The <em>Dhammapada</em> opens with this: </p><p>Every experience is shaped by the mind that meets it. An agitated mind, and stress trails you like a shadow; a settled mind, and ease follows just as faithfully (v. 1-2). </p><p>This is, most straightforwardly, <em>cause and effect</em>.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"819\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:98776,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/208425387?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!zUJR!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3136c74-9377-4565-b7f5-995c2957b9e6_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>The mind is a natural storyteller — constantly predicting, replaying, catastrophising, judging, comparing, often before we’ve finished our coffee. </p><p>The <em>Dhammapada</em> calls the mind “hard to control, flighty, alighting where it wishes”, but emphasises that it <em>can</em> be tamed, and that a watched mind brings happiness (v. 33–36). </p><p>The goal isn’t to silence the inner chatter, but to notice it: catch a spiralling thought, see it as <em>just a thought — a mental event</em> — rather than a verdict on reality, and let it pass instead of grasping at it.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"819\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:741597,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/208425387?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D10j!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb162ef42-3b5f-422c-bbf5-6c4948f2ce6e_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>This doesn’t mean that all hardship or misfortune is the mind’s fault, or that positive thinking fixes our problems — plenty of conditions sit outside our control. But one verse from the text puts it plainly: </p><p>A poorly directed mind does more harm than an enemy, while a well-directed one does more good than your own parents (v. 42–43). </p><p>The conversation inside our own head is the one thing we always get to work with, not because nothing else matters, but because <em>it’s the one lever we get to hold</em>.</p><p>This, fundamentally, is <em>a practice of ownership</em> — learning to meet our thoughts differently, rather than being run by them. </p><p>However each moment unfolds, <strong>the mind leads the way</strong>.</p><h6><em>Note: Verse translations are from The Dhammapada, trans. Gil Fronsdal (Shambhala, 2006).</em></h6><div><hr></div><p><span>At Take A Pause Live on Insight Timer over 25-26 July 2026, we practiced observing thoughts arising and changing in the mind, and reflected on how our relationship with thoughts shape our experiences. We closed the session with a reading from Erin Lee’s </span><a href=\"https://mindfulmoments.sg/books\"><span>Take A Pause: Waking up to a life of clarity</span></a><span>. </span></p><h3><strong>Meditation Practice</strong></h3><blockquote><p><em><strong>Tap Play to Practice Together:</strong></em></p></blockquote><div class=\"native-audio-embed\" data-component-name=\"AudioPlaceholder\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;label&quot;:null,&quot;mediaUploadId&quot;:&quot;ee8bc485-e977-4535-b488-14b1e3ea06f5&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:1325.5052,&quot;downloadable&quot;:false,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}\"></div><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/the-mind-leads-the-way?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">This post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. Upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/the-mind-leads-the-way?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/the-mind-leads-the-way?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div><div><hr></div><h3><strong>The Wholehearted Woman Retreat</strong></h3><p><strong><span>A five-day mindfulness retreat into quiet wisdom and the light within</span><br><br></strong><span>1-5 October 2026</span><br><span>Siem Reap, Cambodia<br><br>*</span><em><strong><span>Early Bird Offer till 31 August 2026</span></strong></em><br><br><span>Led by Erin Lee</span></p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/i